(7770867, 1290158, 30049, '<td valign="top">
I get what you were going for.  I think, outside of the PP, a tighter presentation would have been more pleasing.  The left area of the image, while serving as effective negative space, could have been trimmed.  Take a bit off the left and the bottom; bringing the bird tighter on the lower ROT grid, but still have enough breathing room to not feel cramped.
<br/>
<br/>Just some random thoughts.  :-)</td>', 'I get what you were going for.  I think, outside of the PP, a tighter presentation would have been more pleasing.  The left area of the image, while serving as effective negative space, could have been trimmed.  Take a bit off the left and the bottom; bringing the bird tighter on the lower ROT grid, but still have enough breathing room to not feel cramped.

Just some random thoughts.  :-)', '2024-10-08 06:38:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7770868, 1290407, 30049, '<td valign="top">
The stark contrast in color between the sky and the reflection are a bit off-putting, at least to me.  Makes it feel overworked and manipulated.  Maybe the color is actually that way with the naked eye at the time of capture?  Don''t know.  The other bit that showed some PP residue is the canyon wall (upper right) and the blue sky.  Looks like a strong selection line.  Makes the blue sky, I don''t know, feel more contrived?  Wonder how this would have come across in B&amp;W?</td>', 'The stark contrast in color between the sky and the reflection are a bit off-putting, at least to me.  Makes it feel overworked and manipulated.  Maybe the color is actually that way with the naked eye at the time of capture?  Don''t know.  The other bit that showed some PP residue is the canyon wall (upper right) and the blue sky.  Looks like a strong selection line.  Makes the blue sky, I don''t know, feel more contrived?  Wonder how this would have come across in B&W?', '2024-10-08 06:44:45.000000', NULL, 0),
