<b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b>
<br/>
<br/><b>My thoughts on the image:</b> Guess Who!  I really am glad you have checked the CC box on your photos!  There are only a couple of people who have done it in recent history, but I kinda want to see it revived.  Free Studies are tough.  I just looked back through the ones I entered ages ago, and mine almost always did poorly.  I have one on my front page, but that was an unusually great image that I got while in Arizona at a DPC GTG.I think in an assigned challenge, this one would have been a top 5.
<br/>
<br/><b>My ideas for improvement: </b> Not hugely noticeable, but I feel like the greens are pushed a little too much.  I think that would help the overall image, but there were some really good entries in this one.
<br/>
<br/><b>Where I would have/did score this entry:</b> I think it scored about where I would have put it.  I didn''t vote, but this would have been a 6 or a 7 for me.
<br/>
<br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,
<br/><b>Eric</b>
<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club

My thoughts on the image: Guess Who!  I really am glad you have checked the CC box on your photos!  There are only a couple of people who have done it in recent history, but I kinda want to see it revived.  Free Studies are tough.  I just looked back through the ones I entered ages ago, and mine almost always did poorly.  I have one on my front page, but that was an unusually great image that I got while in Arizona at a DPC GTG.I think in an assigned challenge, this one would have been a top 5.

My ideas for improvement:  Not hugely noticeable, but I feel like the greens are pushed a little too much.  I think that would help the overall image, but there were some really good entries in this one.

Where I would have/did score this entry: I think it scored about where I would have put it.  I didn''t vote, but this would have been a 6 or a 7 for me.

